tokens":1810.8333333333333,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":109.5,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":30570.0,"cache_write_tokens":17771.0,"input_tokens":48347.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1335.0,"requests":3}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion that simulates a base-fetch failure (e.g. unreachable/empty main ref) and asserts the lock EXITS NON-ZERO rather than warning-and-continuing, for both the new complexity lock and the fixed module-size lock.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T6","T9"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The lock FAILS CLOSED when the base copy cannot be fetched — no ::warning::-and-continue'","The correction's whole thesis is that the module-size lock's fail-open on fetch failure is the defect, yet no AC exercises the failure branch to prove the new lock does not repeat it.","No proving command or fixture is described for the unhappy fetch path."],"finding":"AC3/AC4 mandate the lock 'FAILS CLOSED when the base value cannot be fetched' but no acceptance criterion supplies a way to prove the fail-closed path actually fails closed — there is no test/check that simulates a fetch failure and asserts the build errors.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fede5e967c04b7963","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (superseding list), bullets 3 and 4","norm_id":"n77a32ee79685d630","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Implementer writes a lock that fails closed on parse mismatch but still silently continues (or the fetch error path is untested), and CI is green because the happy-path ACs all pass."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State a proving command that forces the fetch to fail (e.g. point the base ref at a nonexistent branch or empty the fetched file) and assert the gate step returns a non-zero exit code.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"medium","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The AC 'The lock FAILS CLOSED when the base value cannot be fetched' has no described proving mechanism. Simulating a git-fetch-of-main failure in CI is non-trivial, and the plan names no test, fixture, or command that exercises the fetch-failure branch. Without one, the fail-closed behavior is asserted but unverified — the same class of latent bug the plan is fixing in the module-size lock.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1ec2757ef272436d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'The lock FAILS CLOSED when the base value cannot be fetched'","norm_id":"n1685779e58a7bfa7","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Factor the base-value fetch into a script whose failure path is unit-testable, and add a test that runs it with an unreachable ref and asserts a non-zero exit.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"medium","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify the semantic lock's behavior when the baseline file is ABSENT on `main` (bootstrap = allow), and ensure that case is distinguished from a failed/flaky fetch (which must fail CLOSED) — mirroring the module-size lock's `git cat-file -e` bootstrap branch.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Module-size lock distinguishes the two cases: `_build-and-test.yml:377-378` — \"`git cat-file -e` distinguishes 'main has the limit file -> compare' from 'main lacks it -> bootstrap (allow)'\"","The plan's semantic table enumerates removed/lowered/raised/added but not 'baseline absent on base'","AC3: 'The lock FAILS CLOSED when the base copy cannot be fetched — no ::warning::-and-continue' — does not carve out the legitimate absent-on-main case"],"finding":"The semantic lock's mechanism does not specify behavior when `.github/complexity-baseline.json` is ABSENT on `main` (the change that first introduces the file, or history predating the gate). The module-size lock it is modeled on explicitly handles this via `git cat-file -e` (main lacks it -> bootstrap/allow), but AC3's 'FAIL CLOSED when the base value cannot be fetched' collides with this: a naive fail-closed treats 'no baseline on main' identically to 'fetch flaked', which would permanently reject the file-introducing change and block every change whenever main lacks the file.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f512393bddcef8594","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"CORRECTION section 'Resolution: the lock is SEMANTIC' and AC3 (supersedes list)","norm_id":"n6b309190784925ad","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["The commit that first adds .github/complexity-baseline.json (base has no such file to parse)","A branch based on history predating the gate is rebased/verified while main already has the file"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a table row / AC: 'baseline absent on the fetched base -> ALLOWED (bootstrap), detected via `git cat-file -e <base>:.github/complexity-baseline.json`', kept distinct from 'fetch failed -> FAIL CLOSED'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["verify command `grep 'complexity-baseline' .github/workflows/` inspects output with `grep` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P9"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["file_impact is empty"],"finding":"No file_impact declared on a leaf work ticket.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2b56a0701da43def","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"n6324407e6516f811","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Record the {path, reason} files this work will touch (e.g. via set_file_impact) so the attestation is scoped to them.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify a bounded retry/backoff (or a clearly-distinct 'infrastructure error' vs 'lock violation' exit path) for the base fetch so a transient flake retries before the lock fails closed, rather than blocking the build on the first hiccup.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T6","T9"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'a failed git fetch of main emits a warning and then runs the cap ... so a change raising 800 to 5000 passes on any run where that fetch flakes'","The plan's own framing establishes that fetches DO flake; failing closed on the first flake with no retry converts every flake into a blocked build.","No retry/backoff/timeout policy for the base fetch is mentioned."],"finding":"The plan flips the module-size lock and the new complexity lock from fail-open to fail-closed on a `git fetch` of main, but never addresses that transient fetch flakes will now HARD-FAIL builds; no retry/backoff on the fetch is specified, so the design trades an insecure fail-open for a brittle fail-closed with a new false-failure surface.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9170f4ab8ca764e1","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"CORRECTION section and superseding AC3/AC4","norm_id":"n74d5004e885885d0","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A transient GitHub network hiccup during `git fetch origin main` now blocks an unrelated PR's CI until it is re-run or an administrator overrides."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add: 'the base fetch retries N times with backoff; only after retries are exhausted does the step fail closed, and it surfaces the failure as an infrastructure error distinct from a lock violation.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan says the CI lock must 'match the module-size limit's posture' (an exact-equality lock: any change fails), but the complexity baseline is shrink-only and AC6 requires legitimate shrinkage to pass WITHOUT an override; an equality lock cannot both reject grows/adds and allow shrinks. The plan does not specify how the CI lock distinguishes a legitimate shrink from an illegitimate grow/add.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2c17154062a85352","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC1 vs AC6)","norm_id":"n4942b2377831991a","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"State that the CI lock compares against main's baseline using the existing shrink-only comparator (allow removed entries and lowered ceilings; reject any new key or raised ceiling), and clarify that 'matching the module-size posture' means matching only the fail-closed + administrator-override behavior, not the scalar equality check.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"AC#1 (lock the file so any change requires an administrator override, 'matching the module-size limit's posture' — which errors on ANY diff) directly conflicts with AC#6 (legitimate shrinkage with an entry removed must pass WITHOUT an override). A whole-file diff-lock like the module-size gate would block shrinkage, which is itself a file change.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1a0b2369f119502f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, bullets 1 and 6","norm_id":"n3c1f4d53aab38453","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Reframe AC#1: the lock fails only on a growth diff (new key or increased ceiling vs. main), not on any change; shrinkage (removed key / lowered ceiling) passes without an override, and the fail-closed rule applies when main's baseline cannot be fetched.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"AC#4's chosen mechanism (assert entry count is monotonically non-increasing against main) is a proxy strictly weaker than the goal AC#5 names (a new function above C901 must fail even if a matching baseline entry is added). A change that removes >=1 existing entry while adding a new high-complexity entry keeps the count flat-or-lower yet admits new debt.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa84a6264ba71cb07","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, bullets 4 and 5","norm_id":"nd3b1558b823828bb","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Assert the committed baseline's key set is a subset of main's baseline key set (new keys forbidden; removals allowed), which is strictly stronger than count monotonicity and directly satisfies AC#5 while still permitting shrinkage (AC#6).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v4","material_f